09199637791573254,0.09251183398756771,-0.0620400229298409,0.03297621169442893,-0.006886181823240743,-0.04784265733263274,-0.04400961564913371,0.03142175211111693,0.061759324876049376,-0.024547207726824692,-0.06728050741907032,0.0552975151235388,-0.007598180474279266,-0.03373432637264648,0.11825004783386092,0.0067217506489091776,-0.06577134822375164,-0.10188893994278377,0.06782141405478524]},{`id`:'chunk_c6f2b6777fba08fce124e53e',`document_id`:'pdf_Guiding-Principles_40a7da28c688',`title`:'Guiding-Principles',`url`:'https://www.niddk.nih.gov/-/media/Files/Health-Information/Health-Professionals/Diabetes/health-care-professionals/Guiding-Principles.pdf',`text`:'22 More prevalent in those with diabetes; negatively affects self-care and outcomes. Consider depression screening and treatment or referral for those with depression. Depression More prevalent and occurs earlier in those with diabetes; negatively affects self-care and outcomes. Increases risk of hypoglycemia. Consider screening for cognitive impairment in older adults who are having difficulty with self-management. Cognitive impairment Diabetes is associated with increased risk of cancers of the liver, pancreas, endometrium, colon/rectum, breast, and bladder.14 Encourage people with diabetes to undergo recommended age- and sex-appropriate cancer screenings and to reduce their modifiable cancer risk factors (obesity, smoking, physical inactivity).15 Cancer Diabetes is associated with periodontal disease, which can lead to chewing difficulties and tooth loss. The inflammation associated with periodontal disease can worsen diabetes control.16 Both diabetes and periodontal disease are associated with increased cardiovascular disease risk. Encourage people with diabetes to receive regular dental care. Periodontal disease Type 2 diabetes is a common associate of fatty liver disease, which can progress to cirrhosis and liver failure. Consider further evaluation for people with elevated liver enzymes, in the absence of other cause, for fatty liver disease. Liver disease Controlled for age, rates of hearing loss are doubled in people with diabetes. Consider assessing for hearing loss and refer for further evaluation as needed. Hearing loss Comorbidity to consider Impact on diabetes or self-care, and clinical considerations GUIDING PRINCIPLES FOR THE CARE OF PEOPLE WITH OR AT RISK FOR DIABETES | PRINCIPLE 3 polypharmacy, and worsen diabetes control and outcomes through a variety of mechanisms, including limiting the time and resources available for diabetes care and prevention. Patient- centered care of those with diabetes goes beyond care for diabetes alone and requires the health care team to regularly consider a number of clinical assessments and related interventions, such as those outlined below.',`page`:22,`page_start`:22,`page_end`:22,`section`:'PDF page 22',`source_file`:'Guiding-Principles.pdf',`source_type`:'pdf',`source_version`:'40a7da28c688',`embedding`:[0.6359403006635562,-0.0028535254609867366,-0.15486731196789733,-0.16401161081214327,0.12538117490190817,-0.009944383166695452,0.05519552990644789,-0.10102022671710606,-0.07697058430454402,-0.01858783898004153,-0.007596714642567229,0.023920326800537753,-0.018643246446845577,-0.14990895703046853,0.1778678386901213,0.08340419014707874,-0.1519509798653806,-0.02866044399664761,0.008815517383917493,0.12902152841999703,-0.051425008811330566,0.04896787239255053,-0.1278803942953388,-0.01519821585434757,-0.02272428080070785,0.09275328278563963,0.030120633435416898,-0.003778448214766914,-0.04264040594535999,-0.06097018783403178,0.00420220518657551,0.014992437287119392,0.01662637883446758,0.037785996880399866,-0.022733078782716444,-0.10444186514898317,0.11951469065714712,-0.045666633611137195,-0.0050677653221575325,-0.03257936367539375,-0.03702065999219181,0.07696386804603246,-0.07085552684933041,-0.0872087772394364,0.05975375029592495,-0.042653461660960505,0.08432463626270716,0.0824904472174819,-0.05679194821430793,0.035895208773632004,0.03028232612298569,0.06266651394235649,-0.1296856562766595,0.03166087239438915,-0.0390021431737826,0.04934892282272552,-0.028779741467716835,0.00651186763949794,-0.038891978192664524,-0.07829096180371456,0.014529326954672354,0.1578459712463466,0.015333732169692763,0.029526958856207555,-0.044870658645962104,0.09342892286552185,-0.19732618746868635,-0.03929939552520043,-0.06360830546753314,-0.023244873642692565,0.003264488177515729,-0.07951189365325588,0.01020958764676707,0.004270672189129761,-0.02170187416398307,0.007135037472477379,-1.9930898067002194e-05,0.015139083786649916,0.01905918442679142,0.024462283854492964,0.019430531556188853,-0.003758675394200434,-0.08208288863838002,0.036926550244026184,-0.020380849950836603,-0.0197685104629237,-0.0240297948271933,0.10817009874023406,0.0003724498156116712,-0.1372213303328057,-0.07971837247152465,-0.03473539076533823,-0.052089088824671906,0.07950502042845353,0.01617669312751244,-0.011251819930174605,0.008347270026575287,-0.021351783985969527,-0.05297579619480242,-0.04873797173786351,0.04417655102208484,-0.07547656084203182,0.09857686980307957,-0.10095884834570742,0.1476844962505609,-0.0030441051762292873,0.04651515495713296,-0.031789943427056114,-0.0432955627818051,0.019652858764838473,-0.06145873924904871,-0.0082211784231711,0.05905099065528873,0.03636508202208231,-0.005497606192463229,0.07977878318431393,-0.05352747600674776,0.05357084426344837,-0.05057256598075792,-0.00781974802996789,0.034401752612601595,0.04330939441149086,0.01536829226981815,0.039821016190519025,0.1295475374303489,-0.07635544000895379,0.0045182163580753205,-0.02690028779909745]},{`id`:'chunk_f8f318223e7f969683acb30b',`document_id`:'pdf_Guiding-Principles_40a7da28c688',`title`:'Guiding-Principles',`url`:'https://www.niddk.nih.gov/-/media/Files/Health-Information/Health-Professionals/Diabetes/health-care-professionals/Guiding-Principles.pdf',`text`:'23 More common in people with diabetes and may exacerbate hyperglycemia and hypertension. Ask about symptoms of sleep apnea and refer those with symptoms for testing. Obstructive sleep apnea Hip fractures are more common in people with diabetes, even though bone density may be higher in those with type 2 diabetes than age-matched people without diabetes. Consider assessment and management of risk factors for falls and fractures, including neuropathy and vision impairment. Fracture risk People with diabetes are at higher risk for morbidity from influenza, pneumococcal pneumonia, and hepatitis B infections. Provide age-appropriate vaccinations recommended by the CDC to people with diabetes. Infectious diseases More common in people with diabetes; may limit ability to exercise. Consider tailoring exercise recommendations for people with osteoarthritis. Osteoarthritis GUIDING PRINCIPLES FOR THE CARE OF PEOPLE WITH OR AT RISK FOR DIABETES | PRINCIPLE 3 Resources Diabetes management • Centers for Disease Control and Prevention: Diabetes Type 1 and Type 2 and Adult Vaccination • National Diabetes Education Program: º Practice Transformation for Physicians and Health Care Teams º Working Together to Manage Diabetes: A Toolkit for Pharmacy, Podiatry, Optometry, and Dentistry (PPOD) º Promoting Medication Adherence in Diabetes • National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases: Financial Help for Diabetes Care Health literacy and numeracy • Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality: º AHRQ Health Literacy Universal Precautions Toolkit',`page`:23,`page_start`:23,`page_end`:23,`section`:'PDF page 23',`source_file`:'Guiding-Principles.pdf',`source_type`:'pdf',`source_version`:'40a7da28c688',`embedding`:[0.6202857308441777,0.06368983431941903,-0.10383621215936224,-0.2712527591006749,0.2057527081106495,0.07145935609296182,0.004678334590990043,-0.1065187752823365,0.01192079276261244,-0.09705033034251477,-0.008283112861226074,0.0846686429424609,-0.0456088482550645,-0.06705511867944586,0.12065458626948024,-0.06516844767248325,0.03165720918177013,0.1422735139