/type-2-diabetes',`text`:'You can develop type 2 diabetes at any age, even during childhood. However, type 2 diabetes occurs most often in middle-aged and older people. You are more likely to develop type 2 diabetes if you are age 45 or older, have a family history of diabetes, or are overweight or have obesity . Diabetes is more common in people who are African American, Hispanic/Latino, American Indian, Asian American, or Pacific Islander.',`page`:null,`page_start`:null,`page_end`:null,`section`:'Who is more likely to develop type 2 diabetes?',`source_file`:null,`source_type`:'web',`source_version`:'c1dc967de5fd',`embedding`:[0.5108279496597665,0.023848264909508407,0.08215705296149829,-0.19129456229438357,0.09988429740819187,0.010980699325874251,0.08536294818558919,-0.06659072485100354,-0.07855898658262697,0.23525084481484734,-0.024057937878813298,-0.06983346411373666,0.23370981029374735,-0.1646370299073583,0.03743906675674234,0.06659393215666809,0.0077570859124131974,0.051818631314713336,-0.20530634177460363,-0.09032487784548031,-0.06634437043307621,0.017581465785139746,0.09824651153949267,0.014047572051438964,-0.20912646427616283,-0.0677076023507587,-0.10968444382749702,-0.04057840436794514,-0.014108569843747499,0.028391597097832164,0.039738714855906694,0.02351380357694341,-0.013896496738785364,-0.009562564488865895,-0.008664088896767662,0.059649145973942906,0.011982046483832968,0.03650073379544654,0.03583818103668061,-0.16306079897057507,0.028083576058652082,0.00035215444784487894,-0.019364680498229005,-0.033752072286753476,-0.005567310295743518,0.02851395813252287,0.01511633372764165,0.031639851312582824,0.11494724201407432,0.03254491582172253,-0.10542703772820705,-0.008180085811011394,0.0463661144485962,0.07226398053585348,0.09958428690523664,-0.144977073382826,-0.09996564970776173,-0.0059138327584259956,-0.05901407293299374,0.022421444987344604,0.03268364386639872,-0.09769757426953173,-0.09009733482652035,0.12148868729938504,-0.04585827099870996,-0.190062858