854218496604,-0.004116444682761591,0.027080939100034545,-0.0950742278272912,0.021660461602709843,0.01709544386014246,-0.021891896015139824,0.026789458769299793,0.05730876483713741,0.017444104589998705,-0.028468866020866526,-0.0602168039684274,-0.05575131791135769,0.02342178477035749,0.026000928774175456,-0.09421000622622483,0.023867380722692382,0.06766971034099463,0.007838810091147987,0.10019753781875605,0.04415593542268031,-0.09319683566009486,0.01619113301431778,-0.01564241616944765,0.011914284959297531,0.0015494206862184223,-0.04954944417130615,-0.011228418883279155,-0.07716859841982174,-0.048792385636093526,-0.00034759085582856735,-0.09340927391637327,-0.0009401053241790485]},{`id`:'chunk_3f308875e253979aabbd9894',`document_id`:'niddk_type2_web_c1dc967de5fd',`title`:'Type 2 Diabetes',`url`:'https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/diabetes/overview/what-is-diabetes/type-2-diabetes',`text`:'Symptoms of type 2 diabetes often develop slowly—over the course of several years—and can be so mild that you might not even notice them. Many people have no symptoms. Some people do not find out they have the disease until they have diabetes-related health problems, such as blurred vision or heart disease .',`page`:null,`page_start`:null,`page_end`:null,`section`:'What are the symptoms of diabetes?',`source_file`:null,`source_type`:'web',`source_version`:'c1dc967de5fd',`embedding`:[0.5946358724704621,-0.07640851403978659,-0.05482990679509483,-0.12392923344907869,0.10787769396617138,-0.07603101369953885,0.13406464500719426,-0.2223731849454757,-0.12265132840371543,0.019945256934840814,-0.014738124654560716,-0.049506648670430566,0.02857643406533861,-0.13992994449250962,0.07349742215583414,-0.06541625664635635,-0.016733429792972567,0.1166414729653793,-0.06489298959705894,-0.004489341144026747,-0.14081621584585177,0.0853250820277335,0.006012429608413734,0.009674490842022713,-0.05092497317710219,-0.009348917200330856,-0.19681430186507273,-0.12571122249936514,0.04617366657410116